

Sub: Minutes of FIGGY BAR RT Conference.

Date: 12/20/90   Time: 22:26EST
Attendees:
[[Gary] GARY-S]
[[Len] NMORGENSTERN]
[[Wil] W.BADEN1]
[JAX]

  Items discussed include forthcoming conference guests Kelly, Haydon and 
  Martens, and Sanderson, and potential future guests, SUN SPARC's Forth 
  bootrom, adding workstations to a SUN cluster, Zen Forth, EDITORS !,
  Forth Dimensions, JFAR.

Minutes:
<NMORGENSTERN> is here.
<NMORGENSTERN> Just we two. It's a little early.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Guess you saw I followed up on some of your guest suggestions 
<NMORGENSTERN> Yes. I think Guy Kelly will be excellent!
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> is here.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Sorry I missed last week -- User Group Board meeting.
<[Gary] GARY-S> I'm looking forward to all three guest meetings
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Yes, so am I.
<[Gary] GARY-S> We already know Glen Haydon calls them like he sees them
<[Gary] GARY-S> Guy and Dean should both provide some perspectives we have not 
seen
<NMORGENSTERN> Wil, was there anyone else at Asiomar that you think
<NMORGENSTERN> would make a good conference guest?
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Several, but let me sleep on it.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Think I will try to get Charlie Johnsen for the one right after 
MVP. There is room to look at chip offerings in light of Harris' decisions
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Richard Haskell gave three outstanding presentations: Teaching 
Forth in a Required Course;
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Implementing E-Forth,
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> and a program to bet on horse races.
<NMORGENSTERN> Idea: Frank Sargent won the Harris contest. You could sound him 
out
<NMORGENSTERN> about a conference on that, but, from talking to him, my guess 
is that
<NMORGENSTERN> he wouldn't. BUT maybe some of the others might.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Do either of you have a number for Dr. haskell - all I know is 
U/Mich, Rochester
<NMORGENSTERN> Oakland College, Rochester, Michigan.
<[Gary] GARY-S> I've had Frank - and I sort of hesitate to repeat on guests
<NMORGENSTERN> I agree, anyway not quite so soon.
<[Gary] GARY-S> I would REALLY like to have a few more lady guests
<NMORGENSTERN> Did they announce a runner-up to the Harris contest?
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Didn't Rob Chapman win (also?) ?
<NMORGENSTERN> The only women I know in Forth are Eliz. Rather and Terry Sutton.
<NMORGENSTERN> don't know if Terry is still programming Forth.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Wait till you see the note I post tomorrow from Koopman
<NMORGENSTERN> (Also Mrs. Miller--I don't remember her first name.
<[Gary] GARY-S> She declined to participate when Dick was a guest
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> (And Linda Web.)
<[Gary] GARY-S> Linda Web ?
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> (An in joke.)
<[Gary] GARY-S> Expand a bit
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Robert LaQuey has some extraordinary ideas and loves to 
expound on them.
<NMORGENSTERN> Yes, very vocal!
<[Gary] GARY-S> Phone numbers ?????
<NMORGENSTERN> (The joke is that Linda Web is one of Wil's pseudonyms when
<NMORGENSTERN> he is in a joking mood)
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Try FIG office?
<NMORGENSTERN> My Asilomar proceedings are in the back room.
<[Gary] GARY-S> I thought there was also a Lori Chavez associated with Palo 
Alto Shipping
<NMORGENSTERN> Has Mitch Bradley been a conference guest? Every Sun SPARC
<NMORGENSTERN> has an embedded Forth. An installed base of 200000!!!!!
<[Gary] GARY-S> Yes Mitch has and has also declined a repeat
<[Gary] GARY-S> His topic was Forth and Unix
<NMORGENSTERN> Yes, I remember now.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> We added 10 new workstations on the week-end and the 
installation had us ...
<[Gary] GARY-S> I have even had Linda Web it seems
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> go into "new command mode" to get the prom version number.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Of course, Forth wasn't mentioned.
<[Gary] GARY-S> How easy is it to communicate with the SPARC bootrom Forth ?
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Very easy if you want to do it ...
<JAX> is here.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> but you don't want to do so.
<NMORGENSTERN> Why not, Wil?
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> It's really just for bringing up the system and debugging.
<NMORGENSTERN> But couldn't it be used in a "regular" way>
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> FunctionKey 1 and A gives you the prompt
<[Gary] GARY-S> Mitch claims it's a full kernel sans mass storage
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Enter b for boot, c to continue, n for new command mode.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> To get out type go.
<[Gary] GARY-S> 'go' not 'bye' interesting
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> It's very extensive.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> 'go' goes back to UNIX.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Mitch also advises they are teaching a Forth cram class to a 
LOT of folk
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Good!!!
<[Gary] GARY-S> It will also be in tomorrow's Usenet port
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> There is mass storage.  You can clobber anything.
<[Gary] GARY-S> That's a lousey plan - especially with Unix
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> That's why I said that you don't want to get into the boot 
Forth.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Think I'd develop a tic knowing the Forth was there yet 
untouchable
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Think of it as universal hardware controller.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> It doesn't matter what CPU or peripherals you have; the boot 
prom can handle them all.
<[Gary] GARY-S> I presume it has some tables and mask bits ?
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> huh?
<[Gary] GARY-S> I presume the periphs are controlled in part with tables and 
masking
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> The Forth is tokenized so that it's the same on all platforms.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> I don't know the details, but presume it's done by issuing 
appropriate Forth words with symbolic names for the devices.
<[Gary] GARY-S> Back to the add-ons. How smoothly did the 10 worksations 
add in ?
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> We took the week-end to do it, and the users were using it 
Monday.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Some path's had to be re-defined.
<[Gary] GARY-S> That's pretty smooth - networks can be a bitch
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> rc.local, fstab, and one other had to be touched up on monday.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> When I want something done right, I ask someone else to do it.
<JAX>  :-)
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> The trick is to ask the right person!
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> (We hired a consultant for the week-end.)
<[Gary] GARY-S> I doubt that
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Precisely!
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> This week is very strange -- I've had two Monday's and one 
Friday already.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> I'm not going to learn vi; a screen editor is fine for 
creating programs, but ...
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> for editing existing files, I will use ed and sed.
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> pmi, what's vi?
<JAX> arf arf arf
<[Gary] GARY-S> I frankly don't know how you can use Unix without vi or emacs
<JAX> Why did Forth never realize full potential of EDITOR vocab?
<[Gary] GARY-S> full screen Unix editor - one of Bill Joy's gifts
<JAX> talk about a "programmable macro language" ... woof!
<JAX> Nothing like F R X U O etc.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Sun work stations have WIMP text editors.
<[Gary] GARY-S> They ALL have ed, ex and vi
<JAX> Wil, you wrote what to my (limited) knowledge is the best Forth screen 
editor ever. Has anyone surpassed it yet? Are you ever going to release t
he update you were working on?
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> I have no plans at present.  (Thanks for the kind words.)
<JAX> Are you ever going to let anyone look at your update?
<JAX> <<< still uses the Congenial Editor!
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> It's essentially the version in Zen 1.1.
<JAX> will have to check that out ... I don't examine the DOS software as well 
as I should.
<JAX> BTW has anyone gotten a FORTH Dimensions in the last three months?
<JAX> .
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> I have, regularly
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> I got one today.
<JAX> aha, maybe mine will come soon.
<JAX> widdle bit late, huh?
<[Gary] GARY-S> My last was Vol. XII No. 4
<JAX> When 4D comes late I'm always afraid FIG finally went broke and no one 
told us!
<JAX>  :-)
<[Gary] GARY-S> Shades of JFAR ?
<JAX> That's different. He *never* kept a publishing schedule! :-)
<[Gary] GARY-S> Didn't keep me as a subscriber, either
<JAX> (( Larry must be doing ok, IFAR picked up FVG tab for several outstanding 
outstanding sumes).
<JAX> s.b., "sums"
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> FVG?
<[Gary] GARY-S> Forth vendor Group
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Thanx
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> (Have to leave a little early. Thanks all )
